WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.827
The final Python step translates some quality rules into code.

00:00:03.827 --> 00:00:09.302
We inspect missingness, verify identifier uniqueness, test simple validity rules,

00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:13.852
and review category frequencies. Assertions are useful for teaching because they make a rule explicit.

00:00:13.852 --> 00:00:22.047
Production pipelines usually need richer logging and exception handling, but the principle is the same.

00:00:22.047 --> 00:00:25.617
Quality rules should be documented and checked consistently.

00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:29.087
In practice, quality rules should be tied to a use case.

00:00:29.087 --> 00:00:35.162
A fifteen-minute delay may be acceptable for a monthly report but unacceptable for a real-time alert.

00:00:35.162 --> 00:00:42.067
Likewise, an unusual physiological value should often be flagged and investigated rather than automatically

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:45.280
deleted. Good cleaning preserves evidence and documents uncertainty.
